# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Lumen server configuration  (copy this file to  server/.env)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# HTTP + WebSocket port for the server
PORT=4000

# Where the client runs in dev (used for CORS)
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Secret used to sign auth tokens — CHANGE THIS in production
JWT_SECRET=change-this-to-a-long-random-string

# Origin that published project links (/p/<slug>) are built from.
# Leave blank in dev — the request's own host is used. Set it in production,
# where a reverse proxy makes the request host the internal one.
PUBLIC_URL=

# SQLite by default (no database server needed).
# To use Postgres instead, change the datasource provider in
# server/prisma/schema.prisma to "postgresql" and set a URL here.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# ── AI build engine ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Choose ONE free provider:  openrouter | gemini | ollama
AI_PROVIDER=openrouter

# OpenRouter — free API key from https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free

# ── If builds feel slow, these are the three levers ──────────────────
#
# 1. THE MODEL ABOVE. The default is 550B parameters. A smaller one starts
#    streaming code sooner, which is most of what "fast" feels like here since
#    the room watches the app being written. Try:
#      nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free      (built for speed)
#      google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free          (26B, only 4B active)
#      nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b:free
#
# 2. REASONING. Every free model is now a reasoning model, and thinking costs
#    time before the first character of the app appears — for a job that is
#    "emit these files in this format", not a puzzle. Set this to "none" or
#    "minimal" for speed; "low"/"medium"/"high" buy deliberation on complex
#    builds. Blank sends no reasoning field, leaving each model's own default.
OPENROUTER_REASONING=
#
# 3. THE DAILY CAP. OpenRouter's free tier allows ~50 requests/day, after which
#    everything 429s ("Rate limit exceeded: free-models-per-day"). Requests are
#    also deprioritised behind paying traffic as you approach it, which reads as
#    "the model got slow". A one-time 10-credit top-up raises it to 1000/day.
#
# Or sidestep all three: run Ollama locally (below). No queue, no daily cap, and
# nothing leaves the machine — the fastest option if the hardware can hold a model.

# Google Gemini — free API key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Usually the best free option: Flash is fast, is not a reasoning model, and its
# daily allowance is far larger than OpenRouter's ~50/day. Check your own limits
# at https://aistudio.google.com/rate-limit — they are per model, which is why
# completions below are pointed at a different one.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Ollama — fully local, no key. Install from https://ollama.com
#   then:  ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:7b
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:7b

# Context window for local builds. Blank = Ollama's default of 4096, which is
# less than a build needs: prompt plus a multi-file app overruns it and the end
# of the app is what gets lost. 8192 is the working figure. It costs memory —
# the KV cache scales with it — so this is the first thing to lower on a machine
# that is short of RAM.
OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=

# Context window for completions. Small deliberately: the prompt is a fixed
# ~3200-character window around the caret (≈900 tokens) plus 160 of answer, so
# 2048 is generous. Anything larger is KV cache nobody reads, and on a small
# machine that is the difference between the model loading and failing to.
OLLAMA_COMPLETION_NUM_CTX=2048

# ── Building from a sketch or a screenshot ──────────────────────────
# Used ONLY when an image is attached, because the best free *coding* model of
# a provider usually can't see. Text builds keep using the models above.
# Leave a line blank to turn image builds off for that provider — the sketch
# button then simply doesn't appear in the composer.
#
# OpenRouter's is a comma-separated fallback list: its free pool is shared, so a
# model can be retired (404) or busy (429), and Lumen moves to the next one
# rather than failing the build. Pin it to a single name if you'd rather be told
# when your choice is unavailable than get a quiet substitute.
# Current free vision models:  https://openrouter.ai/models?q=free&modality=text+image-%3Etext
OPENROUTER_VISION_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free,nvidia/nemotron-nano-12b-v2-vl:free,google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free

# Gemini's default model is already multimodal, so blank means "use GEMINI_MODEL".
GEMINI_VISION_MODEL=

# Ollama needs a vision model pulled separately:  ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b
OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:7b

# ── Inline suggestions (the editor's ghost text) ─────────────────────
# Also a separate model, for a different reason than vision. A completion has
# about a second to be useful, and the big build models above are slow and
# increasingly *reason out loud*: asked to finish `const sorted = items.` the
# default OPENROUTER_MODEL answered with three paragraphs about what the user
# probably meant and hit the token cap before writing any code. So ghost text
# runs on a small instruct model and builds keep the good one.
#
# Comma-separated fallback list, tried in order, like the vision list above.
# Leave blank to turn inline suggestions off — the toggle then doesn't appear.
# Current free models:  https://openrouter.ai/models?q=free
OPENROUTER_COMPLETION_MODEL=google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free,openai/gpt-oss-20b:free,liquid/lfm-2.5-2.6b:free

# Flash-Lite has its own, larger daily allowance than Flash — so ghost text
# firing on every keystroke pause doesn't eat the quota your builds need.
# Blank means "use GEMINI_MODEL".
GEMINI_COMPLETION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# Must be a model you have actually pulled. Note this can differ from
# OLLAMA_MODEL — a 3B is fine for finishing a line but not for building an app.
OLLAMA_COMPLETION_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:7b

# Which provider answers completions. Blank = the same one as builds.
#
# Set this when the two jobs want different things, which on a free tier they
# usually do. A build is occasional and wants the best model available; a
# completion fires on every pause in typing and only needs to be fast. Left on one
# remote free tier, ghost text will spend a whole day's request allowance in a few
# minutes of typing and leave nothing for builds. Pointing it at a local Ollama
# makes completions free and instant while builds stay on the remote provider:
#
#   AI_PROVIDER=gemini
#   COMPLETION_PROVIDER=ollama
#   OLLAMA_COMPLETION_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:1.5b
#
# Needs enough free RAM to hold that model — see "If builds feel slow" in the README.
COMPLETION_PROVIDER=

# ── GitHub ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing to configure. Each user connects their own personal access token from
# inside the app; it is encrypted with a key derived from JWT_SECRET and never
# sent back to the browser. Note the coupling that buys: changing JWT_SECRET
# makes stored tokens unreadable, and everyone is asked to reconnect.
